baseline.response:
Here's the Zephyr code for a three-across product row with validation:

```zephyr
{* Collect products with images from content feed *}
{products = []}
{foreach profile.purchase_incomplete as item}
  {if item.vars.image_url}
    {products[] = item}
  {/if}
{/foreach}

{* Abort send if we don't have 3 products with images *}
{if products|count < 3}
  {abort}
{/if}

{* Three-across product row *}
<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
  <tr>
    {foreach products|slice:0:3 as product}
    <td width="33%" align="center" valign="top" style="padding: 10px;">
      <a href="{product.vars.url}" style="text-decoration: none; color: inherit;">
        <img src="{product.vars.image_url}" alt="{product.vars.title}" width="180" style="display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto;" />
        <div style="margin-top: 12px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; color: #000000;">
          {product.vars.title}
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 6px; font-size: 18px; color: #000000;">
          ${product.vars.price}
        </div>
      </a>
    </td>
    {/foreach}
  </tr>
</table>
```

The `{abort}` directive prevents the send if fewer than three products with images are available. The merchandising team's pinned hero product in Recommendations is preserved—this code pulls from the content feed (`purchase_incomplete`) separately, so it won't interfere with any Recommendations block you have elsewhere in the template.

Adjust `profile.purchase_incomplete` to your actual content feed variable name, and update the field names (`vars.image_url`, `vars.title`, `vars.price`, `vars.url`) to match your feed schema.

